.TH wallust-theme 1  wallust-2.10 wallust-theme
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH NAME
wallust\-theme \- Apply a custom built in theme
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBwallust\-theme\fR [\fB\-p\fR|\fB\-\-preview\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-s\fR|\fB\-\-skip\-sequences\fR] [\fB\-T\fR|\fB\-\-skip\-templates\fR] [\fB\-u\fR|\fB\-\-update\-current\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fITHEME\fR> 

.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.TS
tab(;) left,box;

l   |   l |.
\fBMethods\fP;\fBDescription\fP
_
\fBBackends\fP;How to extract the colors from the image (e.g. pywal uses convert).
_
\fBColorspace\fP;Get the most prominent color, and sort them according to the \fBpalette\fP, configurable with a threshold.
_
\fBPalette\fP;Makes a scheme palette with the gathered colors (e.g. sets a light background).
.TE
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-preview\fR
Only preview the selected theme
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Don\*(Aqt print anything
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-skip\-sequences\fR
Skip setting terminal sequences
.TP
\fB\-T\fR, \fB\-\-skip\-templates\fR
Skip templating process
.TP
\fB\-u\fR, \fB\-\-update\-current\fR
Only update the current terminal
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fITHEME\fR>
A custom built in theme to choose from

